@startuml
!theme sunlust

interface Prototype {
    + {abstract} clone() : Prototype*
}

class ConcretePrototype1 {
    - field1 : type
    + ConcretePrototype1(ConcretePrototype1&)
    + clone() : Prototype*
}

class ConcretePrototype2 {
    - field2 : type
    + ConcretePrototype2(ConcretePrototype2&)
    + clone() : Prototype*
}

class ComplexPrototype {
    - nestedObject : Object*
    + ComplexPrototype(ComplexPrototype&)
    + clone() : Prototype*
}

class PrototypeFactory {
    - prototypes : map<string, Prototype*>
    + registerPrototype(string, Prototype*) : void
    + createPrototype(string) : Prototype*
    + unregisterPrototype(string) : void
}

class Client {
    + operation() : void
}

Prototype <|.. ConcretePrototype1
Prototype <|.. ConcretePrototype2
Prototype <|.. ComplexPrototype

PrototypeFactory o--> Prototype : manages
Client ..> Prototype : uses
Client ..> PrototypeFactory : uses

note right of Prototype
    Declares the cloning interface.
    Usually contains a single
    clone() method.
end note

note right of ConcretePrototype1
    Implements the cloning operation.
    Creates a copy of itself and
    returns it to the caller.
end note

note right of PrototypeFactory
    Maintains a registry of prototypes.
    Provides clones of registered
    prototypes on demand.
end note

note bottom of ComplexPrototype
    Performs deep copy when cloning
    to avoid sharing nested objects
    between original and clone.
end note

@enduml